INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>The Importance of Correctly Determining Corn Seed Rate per Hectare</h2>\n<p>One of the most critical decisions in corn farm management is selecting the variable \'corn seed rate per hectare.\' This figure is not static and is influenced by factors such as seed class (R1 to R5), row spacing, regional climatic conditions, and irrigation system type. Over-planting causes intense plant competition for light and nutrients, resulting in reduced kernel size and the risk of ear abortion, while under-planting leads to inefficient use of farm resources and decreased total yield.</p>\n<p>For a better understanding of the balance between density and performance, it is recommended to refer to the article on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%B0%D8%B1%D8%AA-%D9%85%DA%A9%D8%B2%DB%8C%DA%A9%DB%8C-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">Corn Yield per Hectare</a> to gain a more comprehensive view of the final output.</p>\n\n<h2>Calculation Formulas for Determining Kernels per Hectare</h2>\n<p>The calculation of corn seed rate per hectare is based on two main variables: row spacing (in meters) and the spacing between two kernels in a row (in centimeters). The general reference figure for Iran\'s climate is planting 55,000 to 60,000 viable kernels per hectare, although these figures can vary.</p>\n<h3>Step 1: Determining Desired In-Row Plant Density</h3>\n<p>Assuming a row spacing of 75 cm (common standard) and a seed spacing of 25 cm, the calculations are as follows:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Seeds per meter of row: 100 cm divided by seed spacing (25 cm) equals 4 seeds per meter.</li>\n<li>Rows per hectare: Land width (100 m) divided by row spacing (0.75 m) results in approximately 133 rows placed along the field length (100 m).</li>\n<li>Total seeds per hectare: The practical method is to multiply 100 m row length by 4 seeds per meter (for one row) and then by the number of possible rows from surface area (100 m width divided by 0.75 m spacing). Precise calculation: (100 m / 0.75 m) × 100 m × 4 seeds/meter ≈ 53,333 seeds per hectare.</li>\n<li>If seed spacing is reduced to 20 cm, density increases to 5 seeds per meter and the final number reaches approximately 66,666 seeds per hectare, which is excessive for most varieties.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Impact of seed classification on seed amount</h3>\n<p>Corns with lower classification (R1 and R2) generally require lower density (approx. 45,000–50,000), while late-maturing corns (R4 and R5) require higher density (approx. 55,000–60,000). If you are using new hybrid seeds, always refer to the seed bag label. Varieties with more than 20 ears per main stalk can tolerate higher density to utilize their final potential.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ذرت-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ذرت در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare crop ذرت</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Relationship between corn seed quantity per hectare and irrigation systems</h2>\n<p>Modern irrigation systems such as drip and tape systems directly affect root distribution and consequently seed density requirements. In sprinkler systems, uniform moisture distribution makes medium seed density manageable, but in drip irrigation, water is concentrated around the plant.</p>\n<h3>Drip irrigation and seed density</h3>\n<p>In drip irrigation, it is recommended to use higher seed densities (close to the target maximum, for example 60,000 seeds) because the wetted zone is narrow and plants must be spaced closer together to maximize the use of nutrient resources within the root zone. If you are transitioning to a new drip system, reviewing how to choose the appropriate drip tape irrigation can help coordinate the emitter spacing with the planting row.</p>\n<h3>Tape irrigation and planting next to the tape</h3>\n<p>In the tape system, irrigation is supplied through discrete tapes. If you are using the side-of-the-ridge (Boghal Dozht) tape system, where plants are located exactly next to the tape, you must accurately adjust the spacing of corn seeds per hectare (distance from the tape and between seeds) to ensure sufficient light reaches lower seeds without shading from other plants. To understand the structural differences between systems, refer to the article on differences between side-of-the-ridge and in-ridge tape systems.</p>\n\n\n<h2>Practical tips for optimizing planting and field management</h2>\n<p>A suitable seedbed, adequate seed moisture before planting, and calibration of the planting machine are the three main pillars that, if neglected, render even the best theoretical calculations useless.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ذرت-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ذرت در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for corn</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Hundred-seed weight test:</strong> To convert seed quantity from kilograms to seed count, determine the average weight of 100 seeds. Example: If the weight of 100 seeds is 35 g, each kilogram contains 2,857 seeds. To plant 55,000 seeds per hectare, you need approximately 19.2 kg of seed.</li>\n<li><strong>Competition management:</strong> In fields with sandy soil and drip irrigation, a higher plant density may be required to establish canopy cover more quickly and reduce soil surface evaporation. This helps retain soil moisture for ear development.</li>\n<li><strong>Row spacing adjustment:</strong> If you can plant at row spacings of 80 to 90 cm (for mechanized harvesting equipment), you must increase the in-row seed spacing to keep the total plants per hectare constant, or decrease the row spacing.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Additionally, to compare corn yield with other legumes and vegetables, understanding density variables for each crop helps optimize seed resource use. Studying chickpea seed rate per hectare and influencing factors can provide broader insight into density management in intercropping systems.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<h3>Is there a fixed rate for corn seed quantity per hectare?</h3>\n<p>No. This rate varies between 45,000 and 65,000 viable seeds per hectare, depending on seed classification (EAR), growing season length, and irrigation type. The optimal criterion is maximum canopy coverage before the 12-leaf stage.</p>\n<h3>Does drip tape irrigation affect the number of seeds per hectare?</h3>\n<p>Yes. In drip tape systems, due to moisture fluctuations along the row, it is generally recommended to calculate density approximately 10% lower than reference values for standard drip to prevent plant stress at the end of the tape.</p>\n\n<h3>How can we prevent physical seed deficiency?</h3>\n<p>Always account for the seed germination percentage based on the package label. If germination is 90%, an additional 10% of seeds must be planted to ensure the desired final field density. This calculation must be performed before planting.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ذرت-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ذرت در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare corn</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>Precise determination <strong>Corn seed rate per hectare</strong> It is a composite process involving mathematical calculations, climate awareness, and a deep understanding of the irrigation system (drip or tape). By coordinating row spacing, seed density per row, and moisture management, maximum land efficiency and increased grain yield can be achieved. It is recommended that in the first year of cultivation, a trial section of the farm be planted with two different densities (e.g., 50,000 and 60,000) and at the end of the season, yield and grain quality be compared to identify the ideal variable for your farms.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> Chickpea seed rate per hectare + influencing factors, differences between tape on both sides of cut and plate, lettuce head yield per hectare: influencing factors + methods to increase, pea yield per hectare: comprehensive guide and influencing factors</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d9%82%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d9%86%d8%ae%d9%88%d8%af-%d9%81%d8%b1%d9%86%da%af%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Chickpea seed rate per hectare + influencing factors</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d8%aa%d9%81%d8%a7%d9%88%d8%aa-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d8%a8%d8%ba%d9%84-%d8%af%d9%88%d8%ae%d8%aa-%d9%88-%d9%be%d9%84%d8%a7%da%a9%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Differences between seam-type drip line and plaque-type</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%da%a9%d8%a7%d9%87%d9%88-%d9%be%db%8c%da%86-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Curling lettuce yield per hectare: influencing factors + methods to increase</a></p>','Maize Seed Quantity per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide to Planting and Irrigation Management','Correctly determining the corn seed rate per hectare requires knowledge of seed classification, row spacing, and planting methods. This article reviews the calculation formulas and practical tips for planting corn using drip and tape irrigation to achieve desired density and higher yield.','publish','closed','closed','maize-seed-quantity-per-hectare-planting-irrigation-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
