INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Critical Importance of Drip Line Maintenance in Cotton Cultivation</h2>\n<p>Because cotton is highly sensitive to water stress, irrigation systems require precision and reliability. Drip tape, as a cost-effective and efficient drip irrigation method, has become a standard component on cotton farms. However, one of the primary challenges farmers face is the proper maintenance of these lines. An unmonitored drip tape can become clogged, develop uneven pressure, and ultimately lead to reduced pollination and lower cotton fiber quality. This article examines the technical and practical details of maintaining drip tape for cotton plants to ensure your system operates at optimal performance.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Filtration Systems and Their Role in Preventing Clogging</h2>\n<p>The most critical factor for drip tape integrity is adequate filtration of the incoming water. Cotton is typically grown in clay-loam or loam soils, which can result in suspended solids entering the tape channels. To prevent this issue, the use of multi-stage filters (Disc, Screen, Sand/Media) is recommended.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Disc Filter:</strong> Used to remove silt and sand particles. This filter serves as the first line of defense and should be cleaned once a month.</li>\n<li><strong>Screen Filter:</strong> Used to remove finer particles. If sourcing water from a well, always use a filter with a 120-150 mesh size.</li>\n<li><strong>Silt Filter:</strong> If your water source is a pond or a river, a silt filter is essential for removing silt and debris.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Remember that a filter only works if it is properly maintained. Excessive pressure on the filter can cause it to burst, allowing all particles to enter the drip tape. In our article on basil seed quantity per hectare, we also mentioned the importance of foliar feeding, which can serve as an indicator for system cleaning needs during the irrigation period. However, our main focus here is on filtration hardware.</p>\n\n<h2>Water Pressure Management and Hydraulic Settings</h2>\n<p>Cotton drip tape systems typically operate with mainline pipe diameters of 2.5 to 4 inches and tape diameters of 16 or 25 mm. The ideal operating pressure for cotton drip tapes is between 1 and 3 bar. Pressures above this range cause unstable washing of the tape and increase surface soil erosion, while lower pressures lead to flow stoppage at the ends of laterals.</p>\n<h3>Connection Inspection and Flexibility</h3>\n<p>Drip tape connections to the mainline hose must be completely tight but not stretched. Using appropriate couplings and metal clamps (not plastic ones) in areas where livestock or machinery may pass through extends the lifespan of the connections. Additionally, install a check valve at the beginning of each mainline hose to prevent water from flowing back towards the pump, which can cause pump damage and blockages in the tape due to reverse sedimentation.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-پنبه-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="نگهداری پنبه با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Utilizing fertigation and internal flushing</h2>\n<p>One of the key benefits of drip tape is the ability to perform fertigation. For cotton, the use of aggressive acids such as citric acid or phosphoric acid at low doses can help clean the inside of the emitters. This process should be conducted during the final days of each irrigation cycle to move flow from the start of the line to the end, removing deposited materials from the holes.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Add the acid to the fertigation tank.</li>\n<li>Increase the flow rate to the maximum allowable limit (for flushing).</li>\n<li>Allow the acid to pass through the entire length of the line for 30 to 60 minutes.</li>\n<li>Return the flow rate to normal settings.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Additionally, cleaning the filter tank before each application is essential to prevent deposits from accumulating on the tape. For more details on suitable nutritional compounds for cotton plants under Iran\'s climatic conditions, you can review the guide on Talib seed rate per hectare, which, despite differences in plants, demonstrates similar phytonutrition principles.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for physical maintenance of drip tape</h2>\n<h3>Harvesting and moving the drip tape</h3>\n<p>Cotton is a long-season crop and may require replaceable (retractable) lateral hoses. When harvesting the tape, completely drain it. Never fold a water-filled tape, as this will tear the emitter holes and cause internal damage. Gather the tape on one side and fold it using a strap or a special bag.</p>\n<h3>Protection against animals and machinery</h3>\n<p>Mice and rodents are the main enemies of cotton drip tape. Using polyethylene protective covers or installing the tape below ground in vulnerable areas can prevent punctures. Also, when using a tractor for weeding or planting, ensure that the wheels do not hit the main line or the drip tape.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-پنبه-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="نگهداری پنبه با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Common troubleshooting: Identifying problems and solutions</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Observed</th>\n<th>Possible cause</th>\n<th>Solution</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Flow stops at the end of the line</td>\n<td>Pressure drop, line clogging, or incorrect field slope</td>\n<td>Increase pump flow rate, clean the line with acid, adjust the field slope, or use a larger diameter hose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Water leaks on the soil surface</td>\n<td>Torn line, broken emitters, or excessive pressure</td>\n<td>Repair with a coupler, replace the line, or reduce pump pressure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change in color of water discharged from the line</td>\n<td>Microbiological or chemical contamination (algae)</td>\n<td>Use of hydrogen peroxide or chlorine, cleaning of mesh filters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reduced irrigation efficiency in older tapes</td>\n<td>Internal erosion of holes and deformation of the tape</td>\n<td>Replacement of the tape with a newer, higher-resistance type</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2>SEO and principles of water management in cotton farms</h2>\n<p>Tape drip maintenance is not limited to hardware; it requires smart management. Recording water consumption data and balancing it with rainfall and cotton water requirements at various stages (germination, vegetative, flowering, and boll opening) helps prevent unrealistic stress. Using automated watering systems with hoses and timers improves precision. For a better understanding of how resource management can affect plant performance, you can read the article <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%d8%ac%d8%b9%d9%81%d8%b1%db%8c-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Coriander harvest per hectare</a> Study which indicates the direct impact of precise water and nutrient management on increased productivity.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<p><strong>1. Can drip tape be reused in subsequent seasons?</strong><br>Yes, drip tapes with a thickness of 16.5 microns or greater and UV-resistant structures are typically reusable for 2-3 seasons. However, thinner tapes (less than 16.5 microns) may suffer damage during hot summers in Iran and last only one season.</p>\n\n<p><strong>2. What is the best time for acid flushing of the drip tape?</strong><br>The best time is on the final days of the irrigation cycle or before completely shutting down the system. The flow must be at its maximum to ensure sufficient pressure inside the emitters to flush out sediment.</p>\n\n<p><strong>3. If the drip tape tears during the season, how should it be repaired?</strong><br>Use specialized drip tape clamps (Tape Repair Clamp). These clamps have an inner plastic tube that tightly secures them. Cutting the tape completely or making a cut is not recommended unless the damage is extensive, as this causes uneven flow in that section.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-پنبه-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="نگهداری پنبه با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Crop Drip Tape Maintenance and Care for Cotton</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p><strong>4. Can fertigation be performed directly without filtration?</strong><br>No, never. Directly injecting fertilizer from a separate tank into the drip tape without passing through the main filtration system poses a risk of immediate clogging of the dripper holes. Always inject fertilizer through the pump and the main filtration system.</p>\n\n<p><strong>5. How can I tell when the filter needs cleaning?</strong><br>If the pressure drop between the filter inlet and outlet exceeds 50 centimeters of water column (approximately 0.5 bar), it indicates the filter is clogged and needs cleaning.</p>\n\n<h2>Conclusion: Investing in Maintenance</h2>\n<p>Drip tape maintenance in cotton farms is a continuous process, not a one-time task. By adhering to filtration principles, pressure management, regular acid flushing, and physical care of the tape, you can extend the system\'s lifespan and prevent water waste. Cotton is a crop sensitive to water stability; therefore, any defect in the drip tape directly affects the yield and quality of the harvested lint. For an overview of general principles and critical points in the design and implementation of drip irrigation systems, refer to the comprehensive guide. <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/important-tips-drip-tape-irrigation/">Key Drip Tape Irrigation Points</a> Please review it. By following this guide, you can ensure that every drop of water reaches the cotton roots directly and that your irrigation investment yields optimal returns.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%AC%D8%B9%D9%81%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">D985DB8CD8B2D8A7D986 D8A8D8B1D8AFD8A7D8B4D8AA D8ACD8B9D981D8B1DB8C D8AFD8B1 D987D8B1 D987DAA9D8AAD8A7D8B1</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%B4%D9%86%D8%A8%D9%84%DB%8C%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">D985D982D8AFD8A7D8B1 D8A8D8B0D8B1 D8B4D986D8A8D984DB8CD984D987 D8AFD8B1 D987DAA9D8AAD8A7D8B1</a></p>','Drip Tape Maintenance for Cotton Irrigation: Key Tips for Sustainable Productivity','In this comprehensive guide, you will learn the most important points for drip tape maintenance in cotton farms to maximize irrigation efficiency and prevent unnecessary costs.','publish','closed','closed','drip-tape-maintenance-cotton-irrigation-sustainability',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
